00:12:43.680 --> 00:12:48.720
chance as well. So If Cassie chooses to forgive&nbsp;
young Kang, that may be the push Iron Lad needs&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:48.720 --> 00:12:54.400
to avoid his dark future, saving the multiverse&nbsp;
from adult Kang in the process. Or maybe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:54.400 --> 00:12:58.000
the second chance Kang gets in Quantumania&nbsp;
is at killing Scott… When they meet during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:02.640
the trailer shown at ComicCon, Scott introduces&nbsp;
himself to Kang as an Avenger. Kang’s response?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:06.800
“You’re an Avenger? Have I killed you before?”
So, when Ant-Man starts advertising itself like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:11.600
yet another quirky superhero comedy starring&nbsp;
Paul Rudd, you’ll know the truth. At some point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:11.600 --> 00:13:14.640
that thing is going to take a serious&nbsp;
turn and pull the rug out from under you,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:14.640 --> 00:13:19.760
stomping the main man himself out of existence.&nbsp;
Either that or…y’know…Ant-Man shrinks himself&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:19.760 --> 00:13:33.840
and hops up Kang’s... But that’s just&nbsp;
a theory, a FILM THEORY…AAAAAND CUT!

